# Line endings are part of what this repository compares.
#
# The compose templates are compiled into the binary with `include_str!`, the
# golden fixture and `docs/reference.md` are compared to generated text byte
# for byte, and every file `chaps` writes is compared to what the next `chaps
# sync` renders. A checkout with git's default `core.autocrlf` on Windows
# would hand all of those back with CRLF, so text is normalised to LF in the
# index and checked out as LF on every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.example text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
vendor/marketplace/SNAPSHOT text eol=lf

# Anything that is not text is left alone.
*.gz binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
